  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the Context**\n\nI\'m currently dissecting the prompt and environment details. The key is understanding the constraints: Next.js 15 App Router structure with its specific file organization. This is crucial for creating that responsive UI. I\'m focusing on the core files now: `/app/layout.tsx`, `/app/page.tsx`, and `/app/globals.css`.\n\n\n**Designing the Loyalty Card**\n\nI\'m now diving into the design phase for this digital loyalty card. I envision a metal-textured card with a holographic shine, brought to life with CSS gradients and a floating animation. DeviceOrientation API will create a dynamic tilt effect, while a tap triggers a 3D flip. The back will have a stamp grid, a mock QR code, and customer info. A slide-up menu with wallet options appears upon flip to the back. There will also be a toggleable B2B dashboard. Importantly, I plan for a downloadable single HTML file.\n\n\n**Implementing the Interface**\n\nI am now focusing on bringing the design to life within `/app/page.tsx`, ensuring all requested animations, the DeviceOrientation API (with a mouse tilt fallback), 3D flip, and the 10-stamp grid. The back will feature a mock QR code and customer details. A slide-up drawer will contain wallet options, and a B2B Dashboard Mode will be implemented, adhering to the `frontend-design` contract for the top bar.\n\n\n**Adding the New Elements**\n\nI\'ve incorporated the B2B dashboard toggle into the workspace toolbar as a high-priority addition. I\'m importing `Plus Jakarta Sans` and `JetBrains Mono` fonts using `next/font/google` within `/app/layout.tsx`. The visual design emphasizes a brushed metal texture with milled grain and specular bevels. I\'m focusing on dynamic holographic gradients and a continuous floating animation. I\'m also implementing the DeviceOrientation API for tilt effects.\n\n\n**Refining the Animation**\n\nI\'m now refining the 3D flip animation, aiming for a smooth, visually appealing transition. This involves adjusting the `transform-style`, `perspective`, and `cubic-bezier` timing. The content details are also taking shape. On the front, I envision a minimalist brand logo and a brushed titanium finish, while the back will include customer ID, a 10-stamp grid with engraved emblems, and a mock QR code, as well as a new Desktop orientation control.\n\n\n**Adding the Functionality**\n\nI\'m now implementing the slide-up action menu, which triggers precisely when the card flips to the back. It slides smoothly from the bottom, offering interactive buttons for Apple Wallet, Google Wallet, and email backup. Each button leads to an interactive preview or backup flow. There\'s also a \"Download Single-File HTML\" option. I\'m building a B2B dashboard with a toggle, and it now displays a comprehensive table with customer details.\n\n\n"
