    thinking: "**Inspecting Globals.css**\n\nI\'m verifying the structure of `/app/globals.css`. I\'m confirming that the file adheres to the established framework rule, specifically regarding Tailwind imports and the restriction on CSS variables. No new findings yet.\n\n\n**Refining Styling Strategy**\n\nI\'ve decided to keep `/app/globals.css` as is, embracing the framework\'s constraints. I\'ll put custom animations and styles directly in `/app/page.tsx`, adhering to the single-file component request. Now, I\'m focusing on crafting the `/app/page.tsx`\'s structure with a top bar (`<header>`) and workspace toolbar, including brand wordmark, navigation links, and a CTA button. The details include component layout and placement.\n\n\n**Designing Interactive Components**\n\nI\'m structuring the interactive 3D metal card and inspector layout, aiming for a full 1440px desktop experience that\'s responsive to mobile screens. I\'m focusing on a CSS floating wrapper with a smooth 6-second vertical hover, responding to device orientation for dynamic tilt and specular highlight adjustments. This includes an interactive mode switcher and an export button for a single-file HTML.\n\n\n**Adding Tilt Interaction**\n\nI\'m now incorporating a crucial `Request Motion Sensor` button for iOS 13+ devices, alongside graceful pointer/touch movement fallbacks. To ensure desktop reviewers can test the tilt mechanics, I\'ve added manual gyroscope simulation sliders for Beta and Gamma values.\n\n\\n\\n\nI\'m implementing a smooth 3D flip animation activated by tap/click on the card, with `rotateY(180deg)` and transition effects. The front face features a brushed titanium surface, metallic specular highlight, and a subtle holographic CSS gradient shine.\n\n\n**Detailing Card Back**\n\nI\'m now detailing the card back, focusing on the top bar with customer ID/card code. I\'m structuring a 10-stamp grid with clickable recesses, incorporating debossed numerals and engraved crests for active stamps. Clicking the stamp slots is non-flipping to toggle.\n\n\n**Defining Card Back Details**\n\nI\'m finalizing the bottom row of the card back. I\'ve mocked a unique SVG QR code for each customer card code from the B2B table. I\'m also adding reward status indicators. The right column will hold controls, including a flip button and stamp controls, as well as a tilt simulator and customer selector. A slide-up menu will be triggered when the card flips to the back.\n\n\n**Adding Drawer Interaction**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the bottom drawer interaction, making it smoothly slide up when the card flips. It\'s bound to `isFlipped`, sliding down when `isFlipped === false` and up when `isFlipped === true`. The drawer will have a grab handle and three action buttons: Add to Apple Wallet, Google Wallet, and Email Backup.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
