  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Task Requirements**\n\nI\'m currently dissecting the prompt and `pwa-integration` skill, ensuring I grasp every detail. The immediate focus is removing the wallet buttons (Apple and Google) from the slide-up menu and implementing logic for anonymous local storage generation, as per the explicit requirements. I\'m cross-referencing these directives to ensure alignment and completeness before proceeding.\n\n\n**Implementing Anonymous ID**\n\nI\'ve shifted focus to generating and persisting a unique, anonymous Customer ID upon the initial page load. This ID, formatted as `VSP-XXXX-XXXK`, is crucial, and needs to be permanently saved in `localStorage`. The aim is to ensure its availability across sessions for the `vespera_customer_id`, `vespera_customer_stamps`, `vespera_customer_redeemed`, and `vespera_b2b_ledger` data. I\'m prioritizing the logic for this persistent storage, and rendering.\n\n\n**Generating PWA Assets**\n\nI\'m now focused on the PWA integration, specifically generating the necessary icons and updating the layout. I\'ve to create the `/public/icon.svg` file and generate the various PNG icons for different sizes, as well as the apple touch icon. Furthermore, I\'ll export `viewport`, `themeColor`, `appleWebApp`, and `icons` within `metadata`. The key now is the placement of the \'Add to Home Screen\' button in the slide-up menu.\n\n\n**Prioritizing Installation Logic**\n\nI\'m now integrating the \"Add to Home Screen\" functionality. When `beforeinstallprompt` is available, the button will directly trigger the prompt. For scenarios where it\'s absent (iOS Safari, desktop, iframe), I\'ll implement a modal for installation instructions or native install if available. Core features like \"Email Backup\", UI elements, and language toggles remain unchanged, and I\'m currently creating the necessary PWA assets. I\'m focusing on the service worker and manifest file right now.\n\n\n"
