    response: "The Next.js Digital Loyalty Card codebase has been refactored with the requested changes:\n\n- **Removed Apple & Google Wallet Buttons**: Deleted both wallet buttons from the bottom slide-up drawer.\n- **Anonymous `localStorage` Customer ID & Persistence**: Automatically generates a unique random Customer ID (`VSP-XXXX-XXXK`) on first page load if none exists and saves it permanently in `localStorage` (`vespera_anon_customer_id`) along with active stamp and redemption counts\342\200\224no login or registration required.\n- **PWA Integration & \'Add to Home Screen\' Button**: Configured the Next.js Web App Manifest (`app/manifest.ts`), PWA icons (`192x192`, `512x512`, `maskable`, `apple-touch-icon.png`, `icon.svg`), service worker (`public/sw.js`), and added the **Add to Home Screen** button in the slide-up drawer alongside **Email Backup**.\n- **Core Features Preserved**: Maintained the 3D brushed-titanium card UI, holographic sheen, continuous floating animation, `DeviceOrientation` gyroscope tilt effects, tap-to-flip animation, 10-stamp interactive grid, deterministic unique QR code, B2B dashboard mode, and Bahasa Indonesia / English switcher."
