    captured_user_requests {
      text: "Here is the full initial file tree for the application:\n/.env.example\n/.eslintrc.json\n/.gitignore\n/app/globals.css\n/app/layout.tsx\n/eslint.config.mjs\n/hooks/use-mobile.ts\n/lib/utils.ts\n/metadata.json\n/next-env.d.ts\n/next.config.ts\n/package.json\n/postcss.config.mjs\n/tsconfig.json\n\nThe following dependencies are installed:\n@google/genai: ^2.4.0\n@hookform/resolvers: ^5.2.1\nautoprefixer: ^10.4.21\nclass-variance-authority: ^0.7.1\nclsx: ^2.1.1\nlucide-react: ^0.553.0\nmotion: ^12.23.24\nnext: ^15.4.9\npostcss: ^8.5.6\nreact: ^19.2.1\nreact-dom: ^19.2.1\ntailwind-merge: ^3.3.1\n\nThe following devDependencies are installed:\n@tailwindcss/postcss: 4.1.11\n@tailwindcss/typography: ^0.5.19\n@types/node: ^20\n@types/react: ^19\n@types/react-dom: ^19\neslint: 9.39.1\neslint-config-next: 16.0.8\nfirebase-tools: ^15.0.0\ntailwindcss: 4.1.11\ntw-animate-css: ^1.4.0\ntypescript: 5.9.3\n\nKey file contents:\n\n--- /.env.example ---\n```\n# GEMINI_API_KEY: Required for Gemini AI API calls.\n# AI Studio automatically injects this at runtime from user secrets.\n# Users configure this via the Secrets panel in the AI Studio UI.\nGEMINI_API_KEY=\"MY_GEMINI_API_KEY\"\n\n# APP_URL: The URL where this applet is hosted.\n# AI Studio automatically injects this at runtime with the Cloud Run service URL.\n# Used for self-referential links, OAuth callbacks, and API endpoints.\nAPP_URL=\"MY_APP_URL\"\n\n```\n\n--- /app/globals.css ---\n```css\n@import \"tailwindcss\";\n\n```\n\n--- /app/layout.tsx ---\n```typescript\nimport type {Metadata} from \'next\';\nimport \'./globals.css\'; // Global styles\n\nexport const metadata: Metadata = {\n  title: \'My Google AI Studio App\',\n  description: \'An application built with Google AI Studio.\',\n  openGraph: {\n    title: \'My Google AI Studio App\',\n    description: \'An application built with Google AI Studio.\',\n    type: \'website\',\n  },\n  twitter: {\n    card: \'summary_large_image\',\n    title: \'My Google AI Studio App\',\n    description: \'An application built with Google AI Studio.\',\n  },\n};\n\nexport default function RootLayout({children}: {children: React.ReactNode}) {\n  return (\n    <html lang=\"en\">\n      <body suppressHydrationWarning>{children}</body>\n    </html>\n  );\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /metadata.json ---\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"\",\n  \"description\": \"\",\n  \"requestFramePermissions\": [],\n  \"majorCapabilities\": [\"MAJOR_CAPABILITY_SERVER_SIDE_GEMINI_API\"]\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /next.config.ts ---\n```typescript\nimport type {NextConfig} from \'next\';\n\nconst nextConfig: NextConfig = {\n  reactStrictMode: true,\n  eslint: {\n    ignoreDuringBuilds: true,\n  },\n  typescript: {\n    ignoreBuildErrors: false,\n  },\n  // Allow access to remote image placeholder.\n  images: {\n    remotePatterns: [\n      {\n        protocol: \'https\',\n        hostname: \'picsum.photos\',\n        port: \'\',\n        pathname: \'/**\', // This allows any path under the hostname\n      },\n    ],\n  },\n  output: \'standalone\',\n  transpilePackages: [\'motion\'],\n  webpack: (config, {dev}) => {\n    // HMR is disabled in AI Studio via DISABLE_HMR env var.\n    // Do not modify\342\200\224file watching is disabled to prevent flickering during agent edits.\n    if (dev && process.env.DISABLE_HMR === \'true\') {\n      config.watchOptions = {\n        ignored: /.*/,\n      };\n    }\n    return config;\n  },\n};\n\nexport default nextConfig;\n\n```\n\n--- /tsconfig.json ---\n```json\n{\n  \"compilerOptions\": {\n    \"target\": \"ES2017\",\n    \"lib\": [\"dom\", \"dom.iterable\", \"esnext\"],\n    \"allowJs\": true,\n    \"skipLibCheck\": true,\n    \"strict\": true,\n    \"noEmit\": true,\n    \"esModuleInterop\": true,\n    \"module\": \"esnext\",\n    \"moduleResolution\": \"bundler\",\n    \"allowImportingTsExtensions\": true,\n    \"resolveJsonModule\": true,\n    \"isolatedModules\": true,\n    \"jsx\": \"preserve\",\n    \"incremental\": true,\n    \"plugins\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"next\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"baseUrl\": \".\",\n    \"paths\": {\n      \"@/*\": [\"./*\"]\n    }\n  },\n  \"include\": [\"next-env.d.ts\", \"**/*.ts\", \"**/*.tsx\", \".next/types/**/*.ts\"],\n  \"exclude\": [\"node_modules\"]\n}\n\n```"
    }
    captured_user_requests {
      text: "Act as an expert UI/UX Frontend Developer. Create a responsive Digital Loyalty Card Web App using HTML, CSS, and Vanilla JavaScript in a single file.\nVisuals: Create a realistic metal-textured card with a subtle holographic CSS gradient shine and a continuous CSS floating animation.\nInteractivity: Use the DeviceOrientation API so the card tilts slightly, following the phone\'s physical movement. Implement a smooth 3D flip animation when tapped.\nCard Content: The front shows a minimal brand logo. The back shows a 10-stamp grid, a mock Unique QR Code, and a Customer ID/Card Code on the top right.\nSlide-Up Action Menu: Strictly when the card flips to the back, trigger a smooth slide-up drawer from the bottom containing buttons for \'Add to Apple Wallet\', \'Google Wallet\', and \'Email Backup\'.\nDashboard Mode: Add a toggleable mock B2B dashboard section showing a table with Customer Name, ID, and total redeemed stamps."
    }
    captured_user_requests {
      text: "tambahkan pilihan bahasa indonesia"
    }
    captured_user_requests {
      text: "Refactor the existing Next.js Digital Loyalty Card codebase.\nRemove Wallets: Delete the \'Apple Wallet\' and \'Google Wallet\' buttons from the bottom slide-up menu.\nAnonymous Local Storage: Implement logic to generate a unique random Customer ID on the first page load if one doesn\'t exist, and save it permanently in the browser\'s localStorage. No user registration or login is required.\nPWA Integration: Add an \'Add to Home Screen\' button in the slide-up menu to prompt the user to install the web app as a PWA shortcut.\nRetain Core Features: Keep the \'Email Backup\' button in the menu. Maintain the exact 3D brushed metal UI, gyroscope tilt effects, tap-to-flip animation, the 10-stamp grid, and the unique QR code on the back of the card."
    }
    captured_user_requests {
      text: "Refactor the CSS and Layout for the back face of the 3D Digital Loyalty Card to fix rendering issues.\nFix CSS Mirroring: The text and elements on the back are rendering backwards/mirrored. Use backface-visibility: hidden correctly and ensure the back face container has transform: rotateY(180deg) so the content reads normally left-to-right when flipped.\nFix Layout Overlaps: Reduce the size of the yellow stamp icons. Organize the 10 stamps into a clean, compact grid (e.g., 2 rows of 5) so they do not overlap with the central logo or text.\nMake QR Code Scannable: Ensure the QR Code on the bottom right is fully visible, not cut off by border-radius, and has a solid white background with padding for contrast.\nDynamic QR Generation: Instead of a static placeholder image, use a library like react-qr-code (or an external QR API like [https://api.qrserver.com/v1/create-qr-code/](https://api.qrserver.com/v1/create-qr-code/)) to dynamically render a real, scannable QR code based on the user\'s generated Anonymous Customer ID."
    }
    captured_user_requests {
      text: "Fix the preview crash by completely removing the react-qr-code npm package and any of its imports. Instead, render the dynamic QR code using a standard <img /> tag. Set its src attribute to a public API endpoint, such as [https://api.qrserver.com/v1/create-qr-code/?size=150x150&data=$](https://api.qrserver.com/v1/create-qr-code/?size=150x150&data=$){encodeURIComponent(activeCustomer.id)}. Ensure there are no uninstalled third-party dependencies so the StackBlitz preview loads successfully."
    }
    captured_user_requests {
      text: "Update the dynamic QR Code logic. Currently, it only encodes the raw Customer ID string, which causes mobile scanners to trigger a generic web search. Change the QR data payload to be a functional URL. Update the <img> tag to use this structure: <img src={\\https://api.qrserver.com/v1/create-qr-code/?size=150x150&data=${encodeURIComponent(\'https://api.merchant-system.com/scan?id=\' + activeCustomer.id)}`} alt=\'QR Code\' />`. Use this dummy URL structure for now to demonstrate how the scanner should interpret it as a web link rather than plain text."
    }
    captured_user_requests {
      text: "Attached are the custom visual designs for the digital loyalty card (Front face, Back face base, and Stamp layout).\nRefactor the Next.js 3D card codebase to use these assets.\nAssume these images will be placed in the /public folder named /kartu-depan.png and /kartu-belakang-kosong.png.\nAnalyze the attached back face image. Create a CSS Grid or absolute positioning layout for the stamps that perfectly matches the visual placement of those 8 empty circles.\nAssume there is a /stamp-icon.png (the croissant latte art). Write the logic to overlay this stamp icon conditionally onto the empty circles based on the active stamp count.\nPosition the dynamic <img /> QR code exactly inside the white \'TEMPAT QR CODE\' bounding box shown in the design.\nKeep all DeviceOrientation 3D tilts, gyroscope physics, and holographic overlays active on top of these custom image backgrounds. Ignore if images show as broken links in the web preview, just write the correct source path\n[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_START]\nMedia attachment: User sent attachment: /assets/aistudio/kartu_depan_101f4ead.png (saved in workspace at /public/assets/aistudio/kartu_depan_101f4ead.png). Read it with view_file at that path; in shell commands, which run from the workspace root, use the relative path public/assets/aistudio/kartu_depan_101f4ead.png. When displaying or embedding this asset in code, reference this local file path directly. Only invoke image generation tools if the user explicitly requests creating or modifying an image.\n  User sent attachment: /assets/aistudio/kartu_belakang_a1c1455d.png (saved in workspace at /public/assets/aistudio/kartu_belakang_a1c1455d.png). Read it with view_file at that path; in shell commands, which run from the workspace root, use the relative path public/assets/aistudio/kartu_belakang_a1c1455d.png. When displaying or embedding this asset in code, reference this local file path directly. Only invoke image generation tools if the user explicitly requests creating or modifying an image.\n  User sent attachment: /assets/aistudio/kartu_belakang_sebelum_stampel_e3d362fc.png (saved in workspace at /public/assets/aistudio/kartu_belakang_sebelum_stampel_e3d362fc.png). Read it with view_file at that path; in shell commands, which run from the workspace root, use the relative path public/assets/aistudio/kartu_belakang_sebelum_stampel_e3d362fc.png. When displaying or embedding this asset in code, reference this local file path directly. Only invoke image generation tools if the user explicitly requests creating or modifying an image.\n[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_END]"
      media {
