    thinking: "**Analyzing UI Code**\n\nI\'m deep-diving into `/app/page.tsx`, specifically lines 838-2077. My mission? To meticulously integrate the Apple Cupertino Dark Mode and Bento Grid aesthetic. I\'m prioritizing pixel-perfect execution, ensuring I don\'t disrupt the existing state, handlers, or overall structure. Plus, the Sissi 3 custom component is staying intact.\n\n\n**Preserving Aesthetic Integrity**\n\nI\'m focused on the global canvas and typography, ensuring the core visual elements remain consistent with the original aesthetic. The main container retains its critical characteristics, including background color, text color, and anti-aliasing. I\'m also confirming that heading styles remain intact, reflecting the intended hierarchy and design. Next, I\'m verifying the top navigation bar\'s integrity, paying particular attention to its responsiveness and the backdrop filter.\n\n\n**Examining Control Bar Styling**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the \"Workspace Control Bar\" below the top bar, dissecting its constituent elements\' styling. I\'ve noted the container\'s border and background color, as well as the text styles for metadata (display names, customer ID, and saved badge). I\'m also scrutinizing the language selector and workspace view mode buttons, paying particular attention to their translucent capsule style and active state.\n\n\n**Dissecting Card Stage Elements**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the structure and styling of the 3D Loyalty Card Stage and its associated Bento panels, specifically the left seven-column container. I\'m taking extreme care to keep the Sissi 3D Loyalty Card artwork, QR codes, gyroscope physics, and flip animations untouched. The target is the stage\'s top flip button, which is designed as a translucent capsule. I\'m verifying that its styling matches the provided specification.\n\n\n**Defining Studio Controls**\n\nI\'m now examining the \"Pass Studio\" controls within the Bento container, specifically focusing on styling. I\'ve noted the heading\'s typography and the translucent capsule styles for the \"Pair Motion Sensor\" button. I\'m also scrutinizing the \"Remove\" button, which is another translucent capsule, and the Apple Blue \"Stamp\" button. My focus is on the correct application of these styles to ensure visual consistency.\n\n\n**Styling Merchant Dashboard**\n\nI\'m now implementing styling for the B2B Merchant Dashboard, specifically the Apple Bento Grid and GlassOS Table. I\'ve noted styling attributes for section headings, including font size, weight, and color, along with the subtitle. I am implementing the Apple Bento Grid metric cards, focusing on the grid container and the individual card styles, like background color, rounded corners, and border.\n\n\n**Implementing Metric Styles**\n\nI\'m now focusing on implementing the metric card styles within the Apple Bento Grid. I\'ve taken note of the shadow effect and implemented it. I\'ve successfully applied the metric label styles and the metric numbers\' typography, including the Apple metallic gradients for each card, specifically for \"Total Members\", \"Total Redeemed\", \"Active Unredeemed\", and \"Rewards Ready\". I\'ve made significant progress in applying the various style rules to each of these.\n\n**Designing Search Controls**\n\nI am now proceeding to design search and filter controls for the B2B Merchant Dashboard, noting the styles for the search input field. I am making it full-width with a dark background, a white border, and rounded corners, along with the placeholder styles. I\'m also preparing for the filter buttons and have noted the styles.\n\n\n**Implementing Table UI**\n\nI\'m now implementing the B2B Merchant Dashboard\'s customer data table, focusing on GlassOS styling. I\'ve successfully defined translucent capsule styles with active states for interactive elements. I\'m now addressing table container styling, table headers, rows, and action buttons. The action buttons, particularly the \"+1 Stempel\" and \"Redeem\" buttons, need to adhere to specific color and style definitions.\n\n\n"
