  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the Update Request**\n\nI\'m now diving into the user\'s explicit request. My focus is centered on pinpointing the specific QR code data payload modification needed. The instruction is to replace the current URL within the 3D card\'s QR code on `/app/page.tsx` with a new one. I\'m taking note of the location as the first step!\n\n\n**Implementing the Kasir Route**\n\nI\'m now implementing the `/kasir` route, crafting `/app/kasir/page.tsx` for cashier access. Considering Next.js 15, I\'ll ensure `useSearchParams()` in a Client Component is within `<Suspense>` for static prerendering. I\'m focusing on UI elements, particularly displaying the customer ID from the URL and handling a stamp count. I\'m aiming for a minimalist, mobile-first design, suitable for quick scans.\n\n\n**Designing the Cashier Interface**\n\nI am now structuring the cashier interface. I\'m incorporating a \"Input Pesanan Baru\" form section with quick-select options for common items like \"Iced Latte\" and \"Butter Croissant,\" along with a text area for special notes. My primary goal is the \"Submit Pesanan & +1 Stempel\" button, which will increment the stamp count. I am also planning the Apple-style dark mode styling, utilizing a pure black background, Apple fonts, glass effect navbar, and Bento-style containers for a clean, professional aesthetic.\n\n\n"
